      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُهُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ أَسْلَفَ رَجُلاً دَرَاهِمَ بِحِنْطَةٍ حَتَّى إِذَا حَضَرَ اَلْأَجَلُ لَمْ يَكُنْ عِنْدَهُ طَعَامٌ وَ وَجَدَ عِنْدَهُ دَوَابّاً [دَوَابَّ] وَ رَقِيقاً وَ مَتَاعاً أَ يَحِلُّ لَهُ أَنْ يَأْخُذَ مِنْ عُرُوضِهِ تِلْكَ بِطَعَامِهِ قَالَ \"نَعَمْ يُسَمِّي كَذَا وَ كَذَا بِكَذَا وَ كَذَا صَاعاً\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3939 - Safwan bin Yahya narrated from Al-Ays bin Al-Qasim, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdillah (as) about a man who had advanced dirhams to another man for wheat. When the due date arrived, the debtor did not have any food but had animals, slaves, and goods.\nI asked: \"Is it permissible for him to take these items in place of the wheat owed to him?\"\nImam (as) said: \"Yes, he may specify such and such items for such and such a measure.\""
        ]
      }
    },
